WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:05.690
Landing a role in a Marvel movie means potential
stardom for up-and-coming actors, renewed

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:13.369
popularity for aging vets, and a fat paycheck
for anyone willing to don a cool metal suit.

00:00:13.369 --> 00:00:17.960
But despite Marvel's impact on the modern
movie business, not every actor is keen to

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:21.310
put on a mask and do battle with alien armies.

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:26.720
Here are a few actors who refused big Marvel
roles.

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:27.720
Russell Crowe

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:33.461
These days, Marvel movies are guaranteed to
bring in big numbers at the box office, but

00:00:33.461 --> 00:00:37.460
before the year 2000, that wasn't necessarily
the case.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:42.750
Fortunately, things started to change for
Marvel when Bryan Singer's X-Men first hit

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:43.750
the bigscreen.

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:49.289
It's credited as the film that gave rise to
the modern era of superhero movies, and transformed

00:00:49.289 --> 00:00:54.149
Hugh Jackman from a stage performer into a
Hollywood A-lister.

00:00:54.149 --> 00:00:59.050
But according to the actor, it was pure luck
he got the part in the first place.

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:04.950
At one point, the filmmakers turned to Russell
Crowe to play Wolverine, who was fresh off

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:06.220
the
set of Gladiator.

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:12.260
However, Crowe turned the part down for a
reason that's, well, a little weird.

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:19.470
"I'd just done a character whose animal totem
was a wolf, ya know, which was that fellow

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:20.470
Max in Gladiator.

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:23.420
So I didn't want to be connected with a wolf
again."

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:26.280
Of course, Crowe further clarified his reasoning…

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:27.810
"and plus it's a cartoon,"

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:30.070
"It was a cartoon"

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:32.490
"and I'm not really into those."

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:36.200
But that didn't really stop him from appearing
in Man of Steel.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:41.680
Luckily for superhero fans everywhere, he
did recommend that Bryan Singer go with Hugh

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:45.530
Jackman, who'd previously auditioned for the
part.

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:46.530
Matt Damon

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:51.500
As hard as we try, no one can forget 2003's
Daredevil.

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:56.510
While the Ben Affleck flick did well financially,
critics tore it apart.

00:01:56.510 --> 00:01:59.990
When asked about the film in 2016, Affleck
responded,

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:04.640
"I hated Daredevil so much, you know what
i mean.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:08.500
I did ok, don't feel bad for me."

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:12.530
Turns out that Affleck could've been spared
all that embarrassment if his best friend

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:14.760
had accepted the role first.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:20.330
Matt Damon was offered the part of Daredevil,
and it was a pretty tempting deal, since Damon

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:23.859
and Affleck considered Daredevil to be their
favorite superhero.

00:02:23.859 --> 00:02:28.380
But when Damon was approached with the project,
reportedly he just wasn't impressed with the

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:30.940
script or familiar enough with the director.

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:35.840
Affleck couldn't say no, and has come to regret
that decision.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:42.340
But at least Daredevil's failure inspired
him to get his next superhero movie "right."

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:43.579
Joseph Gordon-Levitt

00:02:43.579 --> 00:02:48.750
Over the years, there have been a lot of whispers
about Joseph Gordon-Levitt and the Marvel

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:53.969
Cinematic Universe, but JGL has denied them
all, from Doctor Strange to Ant-Man.

00:02:53.969 --> 00:03:00.260
Nevertheless, according to Deadline, the actor
was in the running for the role of Peter Quill,

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:05.510
a.k.a. Star-Lord, which he allegedly turned
down to play the character of Johnny in Sin

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:07.280
City: A Dame to Kill For.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:13.099
Which probably wasn't a great choice for Gordon-Levitt,
but we're pretty happy with Chris Pratt.

00:03:13.099 --> 00:03:14.579
Olivia Munn

00:03:14.579 --> 00:03:20.239
When Deadpool hit theaters in early 2016,
moviegoers went wild for the film's raunchy

00:03:20.239 --> 00:03:21.930
humor and bloody shootouts.

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:27.519
X-Men: Apocalypse, on the other hand, wasn't
quite so successful, limping away from theaters

00:03:27.519 --> 00:03:30.980
with a Rotten Tomatoes score of 48 percent.

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:34.709
But none of these numbers really mattered
to Olivia Munn.

00:03:34.709 --> 00:03:39.150
Before signing up to play the role of Psylocke
in X-Men, Munn was first offered the role

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:43.310
of Vanessa Carlysle, Deadpool's "scrappy"
girlfriend.

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:48.200
Munn turned the part down in favor of playing
the spandex-clad mutant, saying that she wasn't

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:51.129
interested in playing the protagonist's "eye
candy."

00:03:51.129 --> 00:03:55.370
Instead, she wanted to be a character with
"powerful abilities", extreme fighting skills…

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:58.790
and a costume that's pretty much underpants.

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:00.120
Mel Gibson

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:07.260
It was a coup for Marvel's movies when award-winner
Anthony Hopkins agreed to join the MCU as

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:10.969
Odin, Thor's father and king of Asgard.

00:04:10.969 --> 00:04:15.380
While he seems like an obvious pick for the
role, he wasn't the only actor in the running

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:17.340
for the Allfather.

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:21.810
In an interview with The Guardian, Mel Gibson
explained that he was asked to play Odin,

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:25.150
but, as he succinctly put it, "I didn't do
it."

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:31.200
At first glance, the action star seems an
odd pick to play the stately Norse god, but

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:36.030
with a solid background in Shakespearean theater,
Gibson probably would've felt comfortable

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:38.190
with Odin's aristocratic dialogue.

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:43.550
Of course, with all the controversy surrounding
the actor, it was probably best for the MCU

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:46.560
that Gibson turned down the part.

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:47.980
Jessica Chastain

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:54.500
Iron Man 3 was the second highest-grossing
domestic movie of 2013, and its praise and

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:56.850
profit isn't undeserved.

00:04:56.850 --> 00:05:01.240
Audiences enjoyed witty dialogue, a brilliant
plot twist, and one of the greatest ending

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:03.890
set-pieces in Marvel movie history.

00:05:03.890 --> 00:05:07.110
The only thing it really lacked was Jessica
Chastain.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:11.780
The studio wanted Chastain to play the part
of Maya Hansen, a scientist who may or may

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:14.750
not be on Tony Stark's side.

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:18.920
Unfortunately, Chastain had to pass on the
role because she was just too busy.

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:20.360
She said to her Facebook fans,

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:24.320
"I know many of you want me to be involved,
and I'm sorry to disappoint you.

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:27.630
Hopefully there'll be another Marvel film
in my future."

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:31.110
Of course, it isn't like Chastain's decision
hurt her career.

00:05:31.110 --> 00:05:34.630
After she turned down the role, it went to
Rebecca Hall.

00:05:34.630 --> 00:05:39.020
Originally, Maya Hansen was supposed to be
the ultimate villain of the film, but someone

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:44.570
up the chain of command ordered writer-director
Shane Black to make the bad guy a dude…because

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:50.020
female action figures supposedly don't sell
that well, leaving Hall in a much less important

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:52.540
role than anticipated.

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:53.810
Joaquin Phoenix

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:58.730
When Marvel Studios was preparing to introduce
audiences to Doctor Stephen Strange, there

00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:00.940
were a few names at the top of their list.

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:06.350
They were allegedly interested in the likes
of Jared Leto and Ryan Gosling, but it seems

00:06:06.350 --> 00:06:10.010
Joaquin Phoenix came even closer to landing
the gig.

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:14.890
The Oscar-nominated star ultimately decided
to pass on the Sorcerer Supreme because he

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:20.320
didn't feel he would do well in a studio full
of green screens, and the role went to Benedict

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:21.320
Cumberbatch.

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:25.470
However, there was a brief bit of time where
it seemed Cumberbatch wouldn't be able to

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:30.560
wear the Cloak of Levitation, as he was already
signed up to play Hamlet in a London stage

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:31.560
production.

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:35.520
To accommodate Cumberbatch's schedule, the
studio ended up pushing back Doctor Strange's

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:37.020
release date.

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:38.340
Emily Blunt

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:42.490
Marvel realized Emily Blunt's action star
potential long before the rest of us.

00:06:42.490 --> 00:06:47.330
As Kevin Feige and Jon Favreau prepared to
shoot Iron Man 2, they offered the English

00:06:47.330 --> 00:06:53.430
actress one of the biggest roles in the Marvel
Cinematic Universe: Natasha Romanoff, a.k.a.

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:54.430
Black Widow.

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:57.610
Unfortunately for Blunt, the timing just didn't
work out.

00:06:57.610 --> 00:07:02.520
She was busy with the Jack Black comedy Gulliver's
Travels and had to pass on playing the Russian

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:03.520
super spy.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:06.260
Which was a pretty huge mistake.

00:07:06.260 --> 00:07:10.850
Marvel still really wanted Blunt to join the
MCU, so when it came time to film Captain

00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:15.870
America: The First Avenger, execs asked if
she'd be interested in playing Steve Rogers's

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:18.310
capable love interest, Peggy Carter.

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:21.970
Once again, the timing was off, and the part
went to Hayley Atwell.

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:27.760
In a 2012 interview with Vulture, Blunt admitted
that she's still open to a superhero role,

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:30.540
as long as she gets to play a hero, saying,

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:35.650
"Usually, the female parts in a superhero
film feel thankless: She's the pill girlfriend

00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:38.870
while the guys are whizzing around saving
the world."

00:07:38.870 --> 00:07:40.100
Matthew McConaughey

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:44.960
If you've seen Guardians of the Galaxy, it's
easy to see why people are incredibly psyched

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:50.190
for its sci-fi sequel, and it seems like any
actor in Hollywood would gladly sign up for

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:51.650
a trip to Xandar.

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:56.960
For example, both Sylvester Stallone and Kurt
Russell will appear alongside Chris Pratt,

00:07:56.960 --> 00:08:02.330
but despite all the excitement, not every
actor is willing to soar off into space with

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:03.440
Star-Lord.

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:08.260
In an interview with Playboy, Oscar-winner
Matthew McConaughey said he was offered a

00:08:08.260 --> 00:08:15.050
role in Vol. 2 but turned it down to appear
in adaptation of Stephen King's The Dark Tower,

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:16.050
saying,

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:20.500
"I like Guardians of the Galaxy, but what
I saw was, 'It's successful, and now we've

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:24.590
got room to make a colorful part for another
big-name actor.'

00:08:24.590 --> 00:08:25.900
I'd feel like an amendment."

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:31.400
McConaughey didn't say which part he was offered
in Vol. 2, though most agree he would've played

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:32.400
a villain.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:37.389
Still, the Guardians sequel should be plenty
of fun even without McConaughey in the film…though

00:08:37.389 --> 00:08:40.760
it'd be a lot cooler if he'd signed up.

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:44.450
"Action and there's the chick, alright alright
alright"

00:08:44.450 --> 00:08:45.540
Thanks for watching!

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:49.139
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:08:49.139 --> 00:08:50.810
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

